    "case_id": "758",
    "case_summary": "A 47-year-old man with no significant medical history lived with his family. Twelve days before death, his father was diagnosed with COVID-19. Two days before death, the patient developed general malaise without fever or respiratory symptoms. His fatigue worsened over time, and he was unable to eat any meals the day before death. The patient was not vaccinated. Physical characteristics: Height 179.5 cm, weight 78.2 kg, BMI 24.3 kg/m².\n\nPatient presented with ST-segment elevation on electrocardiogram. Cardiopulmonary arrest occurred during transport to hospital. No coronary artery sclerosis or stenosis was observed.\n\n- Laboratory Tests:    * Elevated cardiac markers (troponin and brain natriuretic peptide)    * Thrombopenia    * Elevated inflammatory cytokines (IL-1β and IL-6)    * SARS-CoV-2 antigen test positive (>5000 pg/mL) from oropharyngeal swab    - Imaging Studies:    Title: Postmortem CT scan    Description: Dorsal pulmonary infiltrative shadow and bilateral pleural effusions; cardiothoracic ratio 55%- Pathological Findings:    * Pericardial effusion: 70 mL clear fluid    * Heart weight: 426g (above normal range)    * Left and right pleural effusions: 300 mL and 250 mL    * Lung weights: Left 840g, Right 1091g (above normal range)    * Histology showed diffuse contraction band necrosis with several lymphocytes in cardiac muscle    * CD42b immunohistochemical staining showed platelet aggregation in cardiac microvessels",
